<title>UK: Slovak Telekoms closes $170 mln syndicated loan.</title>
<headline>Slovak Telekoms closes $170 mln syndicated loan.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Slovenske Telekommunikacie has signed a $170 million syndicated Euroloan facility with Citibank International Plc, the bank said in a statement.</p>
<p>A total of 15 banks were involved in the transaction, which was mandated to Citibank and ING Barings.</p>
<p>The facility is for five years and the interest margin has been set at 0.40 percent a year.</p>
<p>The company will use the proceeds to expand and modernise Slovakia's fixed line network. -- London newsroom 44 171 542 5887</p>
</text>
